Files: rust/crates/okp-linux-gtk/icons/*
Copyright: the GNOME Project and contributors
License: LGPL-3.0
Comment:
 The symbolic icons the Linux shell resolves for its own chrome are Adwaita
 artwork, compiled into the binary as a GResource and therefore present in
 every installed binary. Adwaita is dual licensed "either the GNU LGPL v3 or
 CC-BY-SA 3.0"; OK Player takes the LGPL-3 option, which is compatible with
 its own GPL-3.0-or-later terms. The files are renamed into an `okp-`
 namespace so a user's icon theme cannot shadow them; the artwork is
 upstream's. Source: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/adwaita-icon-theme

Files: rust/crates/okp-linux-gtk/icons/okp-process-working-symbolic.svg
Copyright: 2025-2026 BeFeast
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Comment:
 Adwaita has no counterpart for this icon, so it is original work drawn for
 OK Player and carries the project's own terms.

